    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0136" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg130"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 67.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commissioner of the United States to China</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                                1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the subject of the
                    interdiction of the importation of arms and ammunition into China, I have the
                    honor to transmit to you herewith a copy of the report of the commission charged
                    with determining the measures which seem necessary for carrying out the
                    provisions of this article of the Joint Note.</p>
                <p>I agreed with my colleagues in reporting these measures as necessary, but, as
                    stated to you in my dispatch No. 39 of March 12 last, I doubt whether any
                    serious attempt is made, except, perhaps, by Russia, to carry it into
                    effect.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d101-a1.xml" xpointer="d101-a1"/>
            </div>
